export function methodologyPage() {
  return `<article class="container prose"><span class="eyebrow">Open about the process · Questionnaire v2</span><h1>How your answers<br>become a profile.</h1><p class="lead">Simple, visible arithmetic. Your summary describes several tendencies in these answers, not a political identity or a match to a real person.</p><h2>1. Twelve subjects, balanced question directions</h2><p>Questionnaire version 2 contains 72 original statements: six for each of twelve dimensions. The quick test selects four statements per axis, 48 in total, with two pointing toward each scoring direction. The full test uses all six per axis, 72 in total, with three in each direction. Questions alternate between dimensions.</p><p>Balancing directions means agreeing with every statement does not push every axis toward one pole. It does not remove wording effects, prove that the two poles are equivalent, or make the questionnaire scientifically validated. Allow about 6–9 minutes for the quick test or 10–15 minutes for the full test.</p><h2>2. Five response options</h2><p>Strongly agree = +2, agree = +1, neutral / unsure = 0, disagree = −1, and strongly disagree = −2. Each statement has a direction: +1 when agreement points toward the first pole of its axis, or −1 when agreement points toward the second. Multiplying the answer by that direction gives its contribution.</p><h2>3. An equally weighted average</h2><p>Within each axis, every statement has the same weight. Add its directed contributions and divide by the number of statements on that axis. The average ranges from −2 to +2:</p><div class="formula">First-pole score = round(50 + 25 × average directed response)</div><p>The second-pole score is 100 minus the first. An average of +1 becomes 75 / 25; all neutral answers produce 50 / 50. In the 48-question version, one response level changes its axis by 6.25 percentage points before rounding; in the 72-question version, by about 4.17. These steps describe the formula, not measurement accuracy.</p><h2>4. Reading your chart and summary</h2><p>The radar chart shows the first-pole percentage: the center is 0%, the midpoint 50%, and the outer edge 100%. A larger shape is not a better result. The paired bars are the clearest way to compare the two poles of each subject.</p><p>Scores from 40 to 60 are described as near the midpoint; this is a wording boundary, not a statistical classification. For scores outside that range, the summary takes up to three axes farthest from 50 and includes every tie at the cutoff, so more than three may appear. This highlights answer patterns, not the importance of an issue to you. It does not assign an ideology, party, country, personality, or historical counterpart. A score near 50 / 50 can reflect neutral answers, opposing contributions that cancel, or both.</p><h2>5. The answers behind a score</h2><p>Newly completed questionnaires retain counts of neutral answers and contributions toward each pole, plus at most two question-and-answer examples per axis. They also record whether the same response was chosen throughout and, if so, which response. They help explain the calculation without retaining the complete answer list after completion. Every answer contributes to the score equally, whether or not it is shown as an example. Counts and examples are descriptive; they are not confidence estimates.</p><p>These details remain only in your browser. Share links include the twelve scores, questionnaire version, and quick/full mode, but omit counts and answer examples. Previously saved v1 results are not given invented answer details. Older or shared results without this local evidence cannot reconstruct it from percentages alone.</p><h2>What this model cannot tell you</h2><p>The questionnaire has not been independently validated or calibrated against a representative population. Percentages are a scoring convention, not probabilities, percentiles, or certainty. Some topics overlap. Wording, culture, language, context, and the small number of statements affect results. Neither test length provides a confidence interval.</p><h2>Versions and independence</h2><p>New tests use v2 with 48 or 72 statements. Saved v1 sessions can continue with their original 36 or 72 statements. Existing v1 results keep their original scores and version; they are not recalculated as v2. Treat different versions as different questionnaires rather than directly comparable measurements. The Portuguese translation uses the same scoring rules but has not been validated as an equivalent scale across languages.</p><p>Our questions are independently written. Our axes and scores are not interchangeable with other websites called 12 Axes. We are not affiliated with 12axes.net, 12axes.vercel.app, Political Compass, or their authors.</p><p><a href="${repositoryUrl}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read the question bank and scoring code on GitHub ↗</a></p><a class="button" href="/political-test">Take the test ${arrow}</a></article>`;
}

export function aboutPage() {
  return `<article class="container prose"><span class="eyebrow">A little less certainty. A little more curiosity.</span><h1>Made for a<br>broader conversation.</h1><p class="lead">12 Axes is an independent, free political self-reflection tool. It begins with a simple idea: a single left-to-right line can leave a lot of your worldview out.</p><h2>Explore without the label</h2><p>We ask about twelve subjects, from economic priorities to the pace of technological change. You receive separate scores, plain-language explanations, and space to think about why your views may differ between topics.</p><p>There is no correct profile. We don’t match you to a political party or public figure, and we don’t treat any pole as a better answer. This project is educational and has not been scientifically validated.</p><h2>Free means the whole experience</h2><p>Both versions, your complete results, image downloads, and share links are available without payment or registration. There are no ads. Optional Google Analytics and Microsoft Clarity help us improve the website after you allow analytics. In-progress answers stay in your browser. After completion, the complete answer list is removed from storage; the saved result keeps scores, contribution counts, and at most two answer examples per axis until you clear or replace it.</p><h2>An independent interpretation</h2><p>Our questions and code were written for this project. Other multi-axis tests helped inspire the format, but this website has its own dimensions and methodology. It is not affiliated with the original 12axes project, 12axes.net, 12axes.vercel.app, or any political organization.</p><h2>Design & illustrations</h2><p>Example result cards use synthetic answers scored by the same 48-question formula as the test. They do not represent real people, measured groups, or political matches. Sora and Poppins are self-hosted fonts under the SIL Open Font License; <a href="/fonts/credits.txt">font credits and licenses</a>.</p><h2>Contact & feedback</h2><p>This website is maintained through the <a href="${repositoryUrl}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">atsince/12axes project on GitHub</a>. To report a problem, suggest an improvement, or contact the maintainer about privacy, <a href="${repositoryUrl}/issues" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">open a project issue</a>. GitHub may require an account to post; using this test never does.</p><p>Project issues are public. Please do not post your political answers, private links, personal information, or other sensitive material. If your concern involves local test data, you can remove it immediately using “Clear my local data” in the footer.</p><a class="button" href="/political-test">Find your perspective ${arrow}</a></article>`;
}

const legalPages = {
  '/privacy': {
    title: 'Your beliefs.<br>Your business.', eyebrow: 'Privacy policy', content: `<p class="lead">We designed this test to work without collecting your answers on a server. Here is what happens when you use it.</p><h2>Who runs this website</h2><p>This policy applies to 12 Axes at 12axespoliticaltest.online, maintained through the <a href="${repositoryUrl}">atsince/12axes project</a>. It covers this independent website, not other political test websites with similar names.</p><h2>Your test answers and results</h2><p>We do not ask for your name, email, age, location, account, or payment details. While you answer, progress and the complete answer list are saved in this browser so you can resume. Completing a test removes that saved answer list and replaces your previous result. Newly completed questionnaires keep the twelve scores, questionnaire version, test mode, completion time, and a limited explanation summary: counts of neutral and first-/second-pole contributions, at most two question IDs and their selected answers per axis, and whether one response was used throughout, including which response if applicable. Those retained examples can reveal political views. They stay in local storage and are not submitted to us, added to a mailing list, used for advertising, or sold. Starting a new test replaces saved progress. Previously saved v1 results retain their original scores; missing answer details are not reconstructed.</p><p>Anyone with access to your browser profile may be able to see your saved test. On a shared device, clear your local data when finished. Private browsing or browser settings may prevent saving, and browser cleanup may remove your data.</p><h2>Optional sharing and downloads</h2><p>If you choose “Copy result link,” the URL fragment (the part after #) contains only the twelve numerical scores, questionnaire version, and quick/full mode. It does not contain contribution counts, question IDs, or answer examples. URL fragments are not included in the HTTP request to our hosting provider. Anyone who receives or can access the complete link can read the scores. We do not create a server-side result record.</p><p>A shared link has no expiry or revocation mechanism. Clearing this browser does not invalidate links or erase someone else’s copy. The link can remain in browser history, clipboard history, messages, or synced devices. Share only if you are comfortable with that. Downloads and printouts are under your control.</p><h2>Hosting and technical requests</h2><p>Cloudflare hosts this website and receives ordinary network information needed to serve and secure it, such as your IP address, requested path, browser headers, and request time. This may be processed in different countries under Cloudflare’s own practices. We do not send test answers or results to Cloudflare through an application API. Read <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Cloudflare’s privacy policy</a> for its infrastructure practices.</p><h2>Cookies, analytics, and third parties</h2><p>With your permission, Google Analytics measures page visits and general device and referral information. For test interactions, we record only starts, completions, image downloads, and result-link sharing actions. These events exclude individual answers, scores, question text, and result-link fragments. Microsoft Clarity captures clicks, scrolling, heatmaps, and session replays on public information pages to help us improve usability. Clarity is not loaded on questionnaire or personal result pages. We do not send answers, scores, or result-link fragments to these services as analytics data. We disable automatic form and outbound-link measurement and advertising features. These providers receive technical information such as your IP address and browser details when their scripts load and may process it in other countries. Read the <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Privacy Policy</a> and <a href="https://privacy.microsoft.com/privacystatement" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Microsoft Privacy Statement</a>. Analytics scripts stay off until you choose “Allow analytics.” You can reject them or withdraw permission at any time using “Analytics preferences” in the footer. The test works without analytics. Fonts are self-hosted; external links are governed by the destination’s policies.</p><h2>Retention and your choices</h2><p>Saved progress remains until you finish the test, replace it, clear it, or your browser removes it. Completion removes the complete saved answer list. The latest result and its limited explanation summary have no automatic expiry; they remain until you clear or replace them or the browser removes them. Use “Clear my local data” in the footer to remove this website’s saved answers and result. You can also clear site storage in your browser settings. We cannot retrieve or restore that information from a server.</p><h2>Privacy rights and contact</h2><p>Depending on where you live, you may have rights to access, correct, delete, restrict, or object to the processing of personal information, or to complain to your local supervisory authority. Because test data stays on your device, you control its deletion there. For questions about this website, contact the maintainer through the <a href="${repositoryUrl}/issues">project issue page</a>. Issues are public; do not include sensitive information. Questions about Cloudflare’s processing can also be directed to Cloudflare through its policy.</p><h2>Policy changes</h2><p>If the service’s practices change, this page will be updated with a new effective date. We will describe material changes here. Analytics requires your separate choice in the analytics preferences; this policy does not grant permission on your behalf.</p>`
  },
  '/terms': {
    title: 'A few ground rules.', eyebrow: 'Terms of use', content: `<p class="lead">By using 12 Axes, you agree to these terms. If you do not agree, please do not use the test.</p><h2>Purpose of the service</h2><p>12 Axes is a free educational self-reflection tool. Its questionnaire and scoring have not been independently scientifically validated. Results describe selected answers at a moment in time. They are not professional advice, a psychological assessment, a definitive political identity, or a prediction of behavior.</p><h2>Responsible use</h2><p>You may use the website for personal learning and discussion. Do not misrepresent scores as verified research, use someone else’s result to harass or discriminate against them, disrupt the service, attempt unauthorized access, or use the website in a way that violates applicable law. The test should not be used for hiring, eligibility, law enforcement, or other consequential decisions about people.</p><h2>No account or payment</h2><p>There is no registration, subscription, purchase, or premium tier. We do not offer paid reports. You are responsible for your own device and network costs. All twelve scores are available after you complete a test.</p><h2>Your control over results</h2><p>You can save, print, and share your personal result. You decide who receives a shared link. Shared links reveal scores to anyone with the link and cannot be revoked by this service. Avoid including information about another person without their permission. Read the <a href="/privacy">Privacy policy</a> before sharing.</p><h2>Website content and independence</h2><p>The website’s original code and questionnaire are made available under the license in the <a href="${repositoryUrl}">source repository</a>. Third-party names and linked content remain subject to their owners’ rights. This website is independent and does not imply an endorsement from any political organization, person, or another testing service.</p><h2>Availability and limitations</h2><p>The service is provided as available without a guarantee that it will always be accessible, error-free, or suitable for a particular purpose. Browser cleanup may erase your locally saved answers. To the extent permitted by applicable law, the maintainer is not responsible for indirect losses or decisions made in reliance on a result. Nothing here limits rights or liabilities that applicable law does not allow us to limit.</p><h2>External websites</h2><p>We link to GitHub and relevant service policies. Their operators control their own websites and terms. Posting a public GitHub issue may require a separate GitHub account.</p><h2>Changes and contact</h2><p>The website, questions, and terms may change. The effective date below indicates the current terms. For feedback or questions, contact the maintainer through the <a href="${repositoryUrl}/issues">project issue page</a>. Do not publish private or sensitive information there.</p>`
  },
  '/cookies': {
    title: 'Just the essentials.', eyebrow: 'Cookies & local storage', content: `<p class="lead">Essential browser storage keeps your test progress. Optional analytics cookies help us improve the website only after you allow them.</p><h2>What the application stores</h2><div class="storage-table"><div><strong>12axes.session.v1</strong><p>Your questionnaire version, test mode, question position, and in-progress answers. Updated so you can resume in this browser; removed when you finish the test.</p></div><div><strong>12axes.result.v1</strong><p>Your most recent twelve scores, questionnaire version, test mode, and completion time. Newly completed questionnaires also retain per-axis contribution counts, at most two question-and-answer examples per axis, and whether the same response was chosen throughout, including which response if applicable. They do not retain the complete answer list. Replaced when you finish another test.</p></div></div><p>These are local-storage entries, not cookies. They are available to this website in your browser and are not automatically attached to network requests. The completed result has no automatic expiration; saved progress is removed when the test is completed.</p><h2>Your choices</h2><p>You can remove these entries with “Clear my local data” in the footer, or use your browser’s site-data controls. If local storage is blocked, you can still complete the test in the current tab, but progress may not survive a reload. Analytics is optional and is not required to take the test. Use “Analytics preferences” in the footer to allow or reject it. Rejecting after allowing stops collection, removes this site’s accessible analytics cookies, and reloads the page. It does not erase information already received by the providers.</p><h2>Optional analytics storage</h2><p>We save your choice as <strong>12axes.analytics-consent.v1</strong> in local storage until you change it or clear site storage. When allowed, Google Analytics may use <strong>_ga</strong> and <strong>_ga_*</strong> cookies, and Microsoft Clarity may use <strong>_clck</strong> and <strong>_clsk</strong> cookies to recognize visits and sessions. Our Google Analytics cookie lifetime is set to one year; provider cookie lifetimes and behavior may vary. We do not enable advertising consent. Browser settings can also remove or block cookies, including cookies outside this website’s domain.</p><h2>Hosting security</h2><p>Cloudflare may use technical mechanisms to deliver and protect the website. See <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Cloudflare’s privacy policy</a> for its practices. Cloudflare Web Analytics is not installed. Optional analytics does not receive your test answers or scores as event data.</p><h2>Read more</h2><p>Our <a href="/privacy">Privacy policy</a> explains result links, hosting requests, retention, and contact options.</p>`
  }
};

export function legalPage(path) {
  const page = legalPages[path];
  return `<article class="container prose legal-prose"><span class="eyebrow">${page.eyebrow}</span><h1>${page.title}</h1><p class="effective-date">Effective October ${path === '/terms' ? '22' : '26'}, 2026</p>${page.content}<p class="legal-related"><a href="/privacy">Privacy</a><a href="/terms">Terms</a><a href="/cookies">Cookies & storage</a></p></article>`;
}

export function emptyResultsPage(locale = 'en') {
  if (locale === 'pt-BR') return localizeLinks(portugueseViews.staticPage('/results'), locale);
  return `<section class="container empty-state"><span class="empty-symbol" aria-hidden="true">✳</span><span class="eyebrow">Your perspective is waiting</span><h1>A fresh place to start.</h1><p>Complete a test to see your twelve scores, or open a shared result link.</p><a href="/political-test" class="button">Take the test ${arrow}</a></section>`;
}

export function notFoundPage() {
  return `<section class="container empty-state"><span class="eyebrow">404 · A different direction</span><h1>This page wandered off.</h1><p>Let’s get you back to the bigger picture.</p><a href="/" class="button">Back to home ${arrow}</a></section>`;
}

function englishStaticPage(path) {
  if (path === '/') return homePage();
  if (path === '/political-test') return setupPage();
  if (path === '/axes') return axesPage();
  if (path === '/methodology') return methodologyPage();
  if (path === '/about') return aboutPage();
  if (legalPages[path]) return legalPage(path);
  if (path === '/results') return emptyResultsPage();
  if (path === '/test') return '<section class="container empty-state"><h1>Your test is loading.</h1><p>JavaScript is required for this questionnaire. If the test does not load, return to the start page.</p><a class="button" href="/political-test">Choose a test</a></section>';
  return notFoundPage();
}

